{"comments":[{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Thanks for the thorough review. Everything is addressed in f7598b55, committed forward:\n\n- **Behavior fixes:** `per_exchange_budget` (300 s), clearing the slot before a nameless set so the old holder's name is dropped, and matching activity events on the lock's device (the secure-mode entity now hears them).\n- **Nits:** the hard refresh honours `slots`; tests use core's real `pin_already_in_use` / `communication_error`; `yalexs_ble.py` is listed in AGENTS.md.\n- **`test_e2e.py`** with a stateful fake of the three credential actions (`fake_service.py`, modelled on Schlage's). It covers setup wri","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:48Z"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"One more forward commit, 5d3d1a22: the Yale Smart Code Handle (`CERES`) refuses `KEYCODE_COMMIT` for slot 100 and up (`NACK 0x3B`, measured on the device: slots 1–99 accepted, 0 is its master code), so the provider now reports 99 PIN slots for that model, read from the device registry, and 250 otherwise. Test: `test_smart_code_handle_has_99_pin_slots`.","d":"2026-11-26T10:50:16Z"}],"commits":[{"date":"2026-11-25T19:41:42Z","msg":"feat: add a Yale Access Bluetooth (yalexs_ble) provider","oid":"4d2a0576"},{"date":"2026-11-26T07:26:10Z","msg":"fix: address review of the yalexs_ble provider","oid":"f7598b55"},{"date":"2026-11-26T10:50:13Z","msg":"feat: report 99 PIN slots for the Yale Smart Code Handle","oid":"5d3d1a22"}],"head":"5d3d1a228404eca5d50ca3a1aea4b23ab2dc6cd5","reviews":[{"a":"raman325","b":"Thanks for this — a Yale Access Bluetooth provider is a welcome addition. Inline comments below; the first three are behavior bugs worth fixing before merge (missing `per_exchange_budget`, activity events dropped for the secure-mode lock entity, stale names on nameless sets), the rest are nits.\n\nOne","d":"2026-11-26T01:25:36Z","s":"COMMENTED"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:27Z","s":"COMMENTED"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:28Z","s":"COMMENTED"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:30Z","s":"COMMENTED"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:31Z","s":"COMMENTED"},{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"","d":"2026-11-26T07:26:33Z","s":"COMMENTED"}],"state":"OPEN","updated":"2026-11-26T10:50:37Z"}
----
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: `per_exchange_budget = 300.0`. yalexs-ble retries an operation up to `DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS` (4) times, each a connect through bleak-retry-connector plus up to three writes waiting `RESPONSE_TIMEOUT` (10 s), so roughly 4 min in the worst case. 300 s sits above that, so the library's own timeouts claim a silent slot first. Covered in `test_provider_constants`.","re":4702859794}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: a set without a name now calls `clear_lock_credential` first (core's `_clear_credential` drops the stored name), then `set_lock_credential`. The set clears the slot on the lock anyway, so the only cost is one extra exchange, and only for nameless sets. Tests: `test_set_credential_without_a_name_clears_the_old_name_first` and `test_set_credential_with_a_name_does_not_clear_first`.","re":4702859800}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: `async_get_usercodes(self.managed_slots | set(slots or ()))`, with `test_hard_refresh_reads_managed_slots_and_the_asked_ones`.","re":4702859804}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Good catch, fixed in f7598b55: the listener now matches the event's `device_id` against `self.lock.device_id`, and falls back to the entity id only when the lock entity has no device. `test_activity_for_the_main_entity_reaches_the_secure_mode_entity` builds both entities on one device and fires the event with the main entity's id.","re":4702859821}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: the refusal test uses `pin_already_in_use`, and there are `communication_error` tests for the set and read paths (→ `LockOperationFailed`). I kept `TestNativeTransportContract` because it's the shared contract every service provider runs; it guards against a future core change that lets an `OSError` through, as Schlage's does. Happy to drop it if you'd rather not have it here.","re":4702859822}
----
